{"text": " Most R-A-G systems are built on English data. Building a production R-A-G system on Swahili documents or on multilingual African business data requires solving problems that most R-A-G tutorials never address. Solving those problems is exactly what makes your portfolio rare. In this lesson, R-A-G systems on African language data sets face three technical challenges that English language systems do not. One, embedding quality. Most high-performance embedding models are English optimised. Multilingual models trade some English quality for cross-lingual coverage. Two, language mixing. Real East African business documents mix Swahili, English, Sheng and local terms within the same paragraph. Three, evaluation data scarcity. Creating gold standard question and repairs for evaluation requires native speakers and domain experts, both of which are less available as contractors than for English evaluation. Apply what you learn in this lesson, and you will see results immediately. Your skills bear fruit.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 4.98, "text": " Most R-A-G systems are built on English data.", "tokens": [50364, 4534, 497, 12, 32, 12, 38, 3652, 366, 3094, 322, 3669, 1412, 13, 50680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.191410886830297, "compression_ratio": 1.3933333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 0.0066469451412558556, "words": [{"word": " Most", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.6, "probability": 0.9595422148704529}, {"word": " R", "start": 0.6, "end": 1.02, "probability": 0.807083010673523}, {"word": "-A", "start": 1.02, "end": 1.18, "probability": 0.5061796382069588}, {"word": "-G", "start": 1.18, "end": 1.4, "probability": 0.9498442113399506}, {"word": " systems", "start": 1.4, "end": 2.06, "probability": 0.986906111240387}, {"word": " are", "start": 2.06, "end": 2.68, "probability": 0.9977171421051025}, {"word": " built", "start": 2.68, "end": 3.0, "probability": 0.9980729818344116}, {"word": " on", "start": 3.0, "end": 3.5, "probability": 0.9